# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ROM data
# Never, under any circumstances. The whole design of these mods is that they
# ship code which DERIVES from your own cartridge dump and never carries the
# dump itself -- committing one would undo that in a single push.
*.gb
*.gbc
*.sgb
*.sav
*.srm
*.state

# ------------------------------------------------------------ other people's
# The engine build, the voxel mod, and any downloaded sprite packs. Not ours
# to redistribute, and large.
*.apk
*.ipa
BATTLE_ART_VOXEL_FORK*/
sprites/
*.zip

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- engine
# The official gen1recomp build, unzipped here so the launcher scripts find
# it. Not ours to redistribute -- download it from the project's releases.
gen1recomp/
gen1recomp-*/
*.AppImage
*.love

# --------------------------------------------------------------- generated art
# Follower frames are built from your ROM on first boot and live in the save
# directory, but ignore the mod-local folder too in case anything lands there.
GHOST_LINK/assets/followers/*.png
GHOST_LINK/assets/followers/*.gif

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------- junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
*.tmp
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- packaging
# Built by tools/package.ps1 and attached to a GitHub release; no reason to
# carry the same bytes in history as well.
dist/

# The pre-conversion patched build. It was an emergency escape hatch, and
# keeping it around meant two play.ps1 scripts pointed at two different sets of
# save profiles -- which is exactly the confusion it was supposed to end.
# Rebuild it from commit 49136ba if it is ever needed again.
splitscreen-legacy/
*/love/
pokemon-profile-backup/
